WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.700
AI generated test cases.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.395
A rushed engineer forgets edge cases.

3
00:00:05.395 --> 00:00:07.467
An LLM reading the spec doesn't.

4
00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:14.133
Give an LLM a user story, an acceptance criterion, or an OpenAPI spec.

5
00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:22.400
It drafts the boundary and negative cases people forget, like the empty string, the unicode name, or a concurrent double submit.

6
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:29.133
The output must be structured, such as Gherkin or typed objects, so it is diffable, reviewable, and runnable.

7
00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:31.667
The pipeline is short.

8
00:00:31.967 --> 00:00:33.067
A spec goes in.

9
00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:36.667
The LLM generates cases, constrained to a schema.

10
00:00:36.967 --> 00:00:38.600
Out come typed test cases.

11
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.833
And a human reviews them before they run in CI.

12
00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.333
Here it is in Python.

13
00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:50.533
A Pydantic model describes a test case: title, steps, expected result, and a category.

14
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:55.185
We ask the model for a list of those, so there is no prose to parse.

15
00:00:55.185 --> 00:00:57.233
A human still reviews before CI.

16
00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:00.700
Here is what a generated set looks like.

17
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.467
Empty email, unicode names, and a concurrent double submit are all there.

18
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.426
Notice the plus alias email.

19
00:01:07.426 --> 00:01:10.033
That's the one a hand written suite skipped.

20
00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:14.267
A signup spec says only that email is required.

21
00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:18.100
The hand written suite covers missing and malformed emails.

22
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.567
The generated set adds a plus alias, and it fails.

23
00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:27.533
The backend strips everything after the plus before the uniqueness check, silently merging two users.

24
00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:29.659
Let's recap.

25
00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:32.667
LLMs draft boundary and negative cases.

26
00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:35.233
The output is structured, never prose.

27
00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:37.533
A human reviews it before CI.

28
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:40.469
Specs reveal what rushed sprints skip.

29
00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:42.967
Next up: self healing UI automation.
